Session 2 (11 AM – 1 PM)
Metadata Filtering

Suppose Vector DB stores:

{
 "type":"loan"
}

and

{
 "type":"insurance"
}

Retrieve only loans:

retriever = (
    vector_store.as_retriever(
        search_kwargs={
            "filter":{
                "type":"loan"
            }
        }
    )
)

Benefits:

More Accurate Retrieval
Banking Example

Question:

Home Loan Documents

Only search:

Loan Policies

Ignore:

Insurance Policies
Credit Card Policies
Score Threshold Retrieval

Sometimes retrieved chunks are poor.

Use threshold.

Example:

retriever = (
    vector_store.as_retriever(
        search_type=
        "similarity_score_threshold",

        search_kwargs={
            "score_threshold":
            0.8
        }
    )
)

Only highly relevant chunks returned.

Session 3 (4 PM – 6 PM)
MMR Retriever

MMR = Maximum Marginal Relevance.

Interview Favorite.

Problem:

Top 5 results may be duplicates.

Example:

Home Loan
Home Loan
Home Loan
Home Loan

Not useful.

MMR returns diversity.

Home Loan Rate
Home Loan Eligibility
Home Loan Documents
Loan Processing Time

Implementation:

retriever = (
    vector_store.as_retriever(
        search_type="mmr"
    )
)
